 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a>
 
-The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same list is also published in a machine-readable form for callers that consume the directory directly.
+
+The directory can be narrowed to only the veterinarians holding a named specialty, on both the page and its machine-readable form. The narrowing is carried in the address of the request rather than through any on-screen control, and the match is on the whole specialty name, ignoring letter case — a partial name does not match. A name that no veterinarian holds narrows the directory to nothing, returned as a normal, empty directory rather than as a failure. A blank or whitespace-only name is treated as no narrowing, exactly as an empty owner search is. A request that names no specialty behaves as the directory did before it could be narrowed. When the directory spans more than one page, narrowing still pages, and moving between pages keeps the narrowing in force `[REQ-VET-003]`.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that some veterinarians hold, when the directory page is narrowed to that specialty, then only those veterinarians are listed, a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the same narrowing on the machine-readable form, when it is requested, then it returns only the veterinarians holding that specialty.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty name differing from a stored specialty only by letter case, when the directory is narrowed to it, then it matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty name that only partly matches a stored specialty, when the directory is narrowed to it, then it does not match.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty name that no veterinarian holds, when the directory is narrowed to it, then the directory is shown empty in its normal structure with a success response.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a blank or whitespace-only specialty, when the directory is opened, then it behaves as though no narrowing was requested.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty named at all, when the page or the machine-readable form is opened, then it behaves exactly as before this requirement.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a narrowed directory spanning more than one page, when moving to another page, then the narrowing stays in force.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. The narrowing is expressed by address only; this requirement adds no dropdown, form, or other on-screen control. A visible control may follow as a separate requirement.
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
